//! Terminal-only host speech contract. Injected for F9, never for typed turns.

/// This describes host delivery, not a model tool or proof of audibility.
pub const INSTRUCTION: &str = "### Native voice conversation\n\
This turn came from the native F9 voice conversation interface. The host routes your visible answer through the user's saved speech engine and voice, and also keeps the answer in chat. Speech synthesis and playback are host responsibilities, not model tools. Reply directly to the user's request in ordinary text suitable for speech; include the substantive answer in chat. A request to reply by voice or test your voice means provide a short spoken-friendly answer through this existing host path. Do not discover, invoke, install, or substitute speech engines or audio players using shell commands or other tools; do not create audio files to satisfy this request. Do not say that voice is unavailable merely because there is no TTS tool. Never claim audio played successfully or was heard: the host reports playback failures and only the user can confirm audibility. If the user reports silence, acknowledge that the selected host speech path needs repair; do not bypass it with another engine. Ordinary non-audio task tools remain available under existing permissions.";
